  "brief": "Sanofi is acquiring Insmed for $41 billion, expanding its respiratory and rare disease portfolio.\n\nSanofi / Insmed (Announced): Sanofi to Acquire Insmed. Sanofi is acquiring Insmed for $41 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal will expand Sanofi's respiratory and rare disease portfolio [4, 6, 7]. Insmed's shares are rallying after the announcement [5, 8].\nClariant / Ashland (Rumored): Clariant and Ashland Deal Rumors. Clariant is reportedly in talks with Ashland to acquire the chemicals firm [10, 11, 12]. The deal is said to be an all-cash deal worth $3.39 billion [13]. The acquisition would be led by Clariant and CD&R [13, 14, 15]. The deal is still in the early stages and no further information is available [16, 17].\nBlackstone / Global Payments (Rumored): Blackstone and Global Payments. Blackstone is in talks to back GTCR's $50 billion Global Payments deal [18, 19, 20]. Blackstone is rumored to be leading the talks [18, 19, 20].\nExpedia Group / Kiwi.com (Announced): Expedia Group to Acquire Kiwi.com. Expedia Group is acquiring Kiwi.com to augment its flights capabilities [21, 22]. The deal was announced on November 25 [21, 22].\nAdvent / Bureau Veritas (Rumored): Advent Weighs Takeover Bid for Bureau Veritas. Advent is reportedly considering a takeover bid for Bureau Veritas [24, 23]. The deal is still in the early stages, with no official announcement made [24, 23].\nAmplifon / GN Hearing (Pending approval): Amplifon and GN Hearing Deal. Amplifon is acquiring GN Hearing [25]. Amplifon has secured a €1.2 billion credit facility [25].\nAFC Industries / Barnhart Bolt (Announced): AFC Industries Acquires Barnhart Bolt. AFC Industries has acquired Barnhart Bolt [26]. The acquisition adds six branches to AFC Industries [26]. The deal was announced [26].\nINDEXO / DelfinGroup (Announced): INDEXO to Acquire DelfinGroup. INDEXO is acquiring DelfinGroup [27]. The takeover bid will begin on November 27 [27].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Pearland expands industrial footprint with new developments [28].\n- M&A in the Industrials Sector Looks Set for a Robust 2027 [29].\n- After $32 billion Google deal, Wiz founders face multibillion-dollar tax demand in Israel [30].",
